# Repo-root .dockerignore
# Applies to any docker build with context = repo root.
# Currently: apps/sim-capacity/Dockerfile, apps/hcc-agent-host/Dockerfile, AND
# data-platform/scripts/po-agent/corpus/Dockerfile.
# apps/hcc-app-fluent/Dockerfile builds from apps/hcc-app-fluent/ context, so
# this file does not apply to that build.
#
# Allowlist approach: exclude everything, then explicitly re-include what each
# Dockerfile needs. Keeps ACR build context small (seconds vs minutes).

*

# sim-capacity image build
!apps/sim-capacity/Dockerfile
!apps/sim-capacity/pyproject.toml
!apps/sim-capacity/src/
apps/sim-capacity/src/**/__pycache__
apps/sim-capacity/src/**/*.pyc
apps/sim-capacity/src/**/*.egg-info

# hcc-agent-host image build (Sprint 13 T5 — Container Apps agent-host)
# The Dockerfile copies pyproject.toml + src/ (app source) + agents/ (runtime
# prompt packs baked into the image at build time, per AGENTS.md).
!apps/hcc-agent-host/Dockerfile
!apps/hcc-agent-host/pyproject.toml
!apps/hcc-agent-host/src/
!agents/
!data-platform/decision/
apps/hcc-agent-host/src/**/__pycache__
apps/hcc-agent-host/src/**/*.pyc
apps/hcc-agent-host/src/**/*.egg-info
agents/**/__pycache__
data-platform/decision/**/__pycache__
data-platform/decision/**/*.pyc

# Golden-source capacity CSVs consumed by calibration modules at runtime
# (moved from docs/reviews/2026-06-29-ama-capacity-metadata-review/ in Sprint 22 P1a)
!data/master-data/capacity/*.csv

# po-agent corpus-refresh image build (data-platform/scripts/po-agent/corpus/Dockerfile,
# built by .github/workflows/po-agent-corpus-build.yml)
!data-platform/scripts/po-agent/corpus/
data-platform/scripts/po-agent/corpus/**/__pycache__
data-platform/scripts/po-agent/corpus/**/*.pyc
data-platform/scripts/po-agent/corpus/.pytest_cache
data-platform/scripts/po-agent/corpus/tests

# docs/ corpus source tree baked into the po-agent corpus-refresh image.
# snapshot.py's snapshot_tree() only globs docs/**/*.md, so keep every .md
# file but drop the non-.md binary bulk it never reads: screenshots,
# prototype HTML/assets and photos under superpowers/ideas/**, logos/icons
# under brandkit/**, and review attachments under reviews/**.
!docs/
docs/superpowers/ideas/
!docs/superpowers/ideas/**/*.md
docs/brandkit/
!docs/brandkit/**/*.md
docs/reviews/**/*.xlsx
docs/reviews/**/*.png
docs/reviews/**/*.pdf
docs/reviews/**/*.docx
